<!-- Section 1: Why Early Assessment Matters -->
<section class="py-5 bg-white border-top border-bottom" id="about">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1140px;">
    <div class="text-center max-w-700 mx-auto mb-5">
      <span class="badge bg-light text-muted border px-3 py-1 mb-2">The Clinical Imperative</span>
      <h2 class="h2 fw-bold">Why Early Nutritional Risk Assessment Matters</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">
        Malnutrition is a complex, multi-factorial condition driven by inadequate intake, monotonous diets, 
        chronic health conditions, and socioeconomic disparities.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-4">
      <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="feature-pillar-box">
          <div class="pillar-icon-circle">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2a4 4 0 0 1 4 4c0 1.95-1.4 3.58-3.25 3.93L12 18"/><path d="m16 14 4-2-4-2"/><path d="m8 14-4-2 4-2"/><circle cx="12" cy="19" r="2"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="h5 fw-bold mb-2">Overcoming Single-Metric Blindspots</h3>
          <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
            Traditional clinical screenings rely overwhelmingly on Body Mass Index (BMI). 
            However, individuals with normal or elevated BMI can still suffer from micronutrient deficiencies, sarcopenia, 
            or poor dietary quality that single-indicator measurements miss.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="feature-pillar-box">
          <div class="pillar-icon-circle">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 12h-4l-3 9L9 3l-3 9H2"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="h5 fw-bold mb-2">Preventative Clinical Stratification</h3>
          <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
            Stratifying patients into differentiated risk cohorts enables healthcare providers to prioritize 
            targeted nutritional counseling and proactive interventions before acute clinical complications occur.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-4">
        <div class="feature-pillar-box">
          <div class="pillar-icon-circle">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="2" y1="12" x2="22" y2="12"/><path d="M12 2a15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4-10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4-10z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="h5 fw-bold mb-2">Scalable Public Health Decision Support</h3>
          <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
            By collecting non-invasive demographic, dietary diversity, and lifestyle parameters, 
            NutriRisk AI can be deployed in community health settings without requiring invasive or expensive laboratory equipment.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Section 2: Stratification Tiers Explained -->
<section class="py-5" style="background-color: var(--bg-page);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1140px;">
    <div class="text-center mb-5">
